<title>SWITZERLAND: FIGURE SKATING-TARA LIPINSKI'S COMPETITION RECORD.</title>
<headline>FIGURE SKATING-TARA LIPINSKI'S COMPETITION RECORD.</headline>
<dateline>LAUSANNE, Switzerland 1997-03-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Competition</p>
<p>record of Tara Lipinski, who became the youngest-ever world</p>
<p>women's figure skating champion on Saturday:</p>
<p>1994 Southwestern Novice - 1st</p>
<p>1994 Midwestern Novice - 1st</p>
<p>1994 National Novice - 2nd</p>
<p>1994 U.S. Olympic Festival - 1st</p>
<p>1994 Blue Swords - 1st</p>
<p>1995 World Junior Championships - 4th</p>
<p>1995 National Juniors - 2nd</p>
<p>1995 Nebelhorn Trophy - 4th</p>
<p>1996 World Junior selections competition - 2nd</p>
<p>1996 World Juniors - 5th</p>
<p>1996 South Atlantic Juniors - 1st</p>
<p>1996 National Championships - 3rd</p>
<p>1996 World Championships - 15th</p>
<p>1996 Skate Canada - 2nd</p>
<p>1996 Trophee Lalique - 3rd</p>
<p>1996 Nations Cup - 2nd</p>
<p>1997 National Championships - 1st</p>
<p>1997 Champions Series final - 1st</p>
<p>1997 World Championships - 1st.</p>
</text>
